1
00:00:00,800 --> 00:00:02,787
New hires learn on real customers.

2
00:00:02,787 --> 00:00:07,403
Role-play needs senior staff nobody can spare, and one wrong promise can cost a

3
00:00:07,403 --> 00:00:08,280
company dearly.

4
00:00:09,996 --> 00:00:13,742
SkillCoach turns a company's own knowledge into realistic practice

5
00:00:13,742 --> 00:00:16,636
conversations, powered by Gemini 4 on Google Cloud.

6
00:00:17,242 --> 00:00:20,642
An admin uploads product brochures and policies.

7
00:00:22,136 --> 00:00:27,576
Gemini 4 reads those documents and proposes realistic customer types.

8
00:00:30,443 --> 00:00:35,483
Every objection and hidden need links back to the passage it came from.

9
00:00:36,068 --> 00:00:38,626
A trainer checks the sources and approves.

10
00:00:38,626 --> 00:00:41,428
Only approved customers are used for practice.

11
00:00:44,235 --> 00:00:46,296
Scenarios are built the same way.

12
00:00:46,296 --> 00:00:51,294
The goal, the compliance rules and the scoring rubric each point to a source, so

13
00:00:51,294 --> 00:00:54,355
a trainer can check every rule before it is used.

14
00:00:57,539 --> 00:01:00,214
Now a new insurance advisor meets Mr.

15
00:01:00,214 --> 00:01:05,202
Tan, a cautious retiree, as a 3D customer who reacts to every answer.

16
00:01:05,202 --> 00:01:07,299
His first question is a trap.

17
00:01:09,945 --> 00:01:11,690
Here's the costly mistake:

18
00:01:11,690 --> 00:01:13,702
promising a guaranteed return.

19
00:01:13,702 --> 00:01:19,070
Before it reaches the customer, the Compliance Guard stops it, quotes the words,

20
00:01:19,070 --> 00:01:20,345
and names the rule.

21
00:01:20,708 --> 00:01:22,896
Send it anyway, and trust drops.

22
00:01:22,896 --> 00:01:24,948
The coach suggests a way back.

23
00:01:35,976 --> 00:01:38,456
Pressure selling is flagged inline too.

24
00:01:46,716 --> 00:01:48,340
An honest answer works better.

25
00:01:48,340 --> 00:01:53,156
The customer only states facts from the company's documents, with sources on every reply.

26
00:02:04,542 --> 00:02:07,579
Each turn runs a pipeline of Gemini agents:

27
00:02:07,579 --> 00:02:12,382
compliance judge, customer, grounding check, trust model, and coach.

28
00:02:19,485 --> 00:02:21,565
Now, the report.

29
00:02:25,596 --> 00:02:29,233
One forbidden promise fails the session, however good the rest was.

30
00:02:29,233 --> 00:02:31,676
The overall score cannot go above fifty-nine.

31
00:02:32,028 --> 00:02:37,842
Every score quotes the trainee's own words, verified against the transcript.

32
00:02:37,842 --> 00:02:39,908
No evidence, no high score.

33
00:02:40,269 --> 00:02:43,720
Each violation names the rule and jumps to the exact turn.

34
00:02:43,720 --> 00:02:47,349
Strengths and next steps turn the grade into a coaching plan.

35
00:02:49,485 --> 00:02:52,815
Managers see aggregates, never transcripts:

36
00:02:52,815 --> 00:02:56,997
skill gaps, broken rules, and who is ready to go live.

37
00:02:56,997 --> 00:02:59,165
Sample team data is labeled.

38
00:03:01,238 --> 00:03:03,842
Under the hood, it's all Google Cloud.

39
00:03:03,842 --> 00:03:08,640
Firebase Hosting serves the app, and the web and API run on Cloud Run.

40
00:03:08,640 --> 00:03:12,683
Firestore stores documents, personas, sessions and reports.

41
00:03:12,683 --> 00:03:15,561
Seven Gemini agent roles run on Vertex AI:

42
00:03:15,561 --> 00:03:21,318
Gemini 4 Argon for the customer, builder and report, Flash-Lite for the fast checks.

43
00:03:21,768 --> 00:03:22,937
The future of work:

44
00:03:22,937 --> 00:03:28,288
a tireless practice partner for every new hire, built from the company's own knowledge.

45
00:03:29,888 --> 00:03:30,662
SkillCoach.

46
00:03:30,662 --> 00:03:33,688
Practice the conversation before it counts.
